  "title": "Google Fines €403m in Ireland Over EU Location Data Violations",
  "summary": "The Irish Data Protection Commission (DPC) fined Google €403m (USD 463m) for breaching EU location data rules, citing issues with how Google mishandled user data. The fine follows a six-year investigation into the company's handling of location tracking and privacy compliance.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Google was fined €403m (USD 463m) by Ireland's Data Protection Commission (DPC) following complaints about data misuse.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The fine comes after the DPC investigated Google's handling of location data and found it failed to process personal information lawfully or fairly.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The investigation, which started six years ago, examined how Google applied EU privacy rules.",
      "confidence": 0.95
